# Settings for the nightly (scripts/chain/nightly.mjs) and its morning report
# (scripts/chain/report.mjs). scripts/chain/install-nightly.sh writes it from
# this example with CHAIN_ROOT filled in. KEY=VALUE, no expansion; the
# process environment wins over this file. Keep it 0600.
#
# Since #361 (2026-11-18) the night is an export and a push: the private main,
# exported the way a release is, goes to the public repository's `nightly`
# branch as one commit, and GitHub tests it there and builds the nightly
# image and desktop packages from it. Nothing heavy runs on this host.

# ── the nightly's own place ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Its directory: the checkout of the private repository (src/), the clone of
# the public one the export is made in (public/), the state (nightly/:
# tonight.json, history.jsonl, state.json, the night's logs) and the
# installed scripts (bin/).
CHAIN_ROOT=/var/lib/filex-nightly
# The branch, and the remote of the checkout in $CHAIN_ROOT/src.
NIGHTLY_BRANCH=main
# NIGHTLY_REMOTE_NAME=origin
# The time zone the night is named in: the commit's Nightly-Date, the
# version (0.62.0-nightly.YYYYMMDD+commit) and the report.
NIGHTLY_TZ=Europe/Istanbul
# Nights kept in history.jsonl.
# NIGHTLY_KEEP_HISTORY=120

# ── the push ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Who the night's commit is by (author and committer): the account the public
# repository's commits are by, "Name <address>". Required: the code names
# nobody, and a night without it pushes nothing.
NIGHTLY_COMMIT_AUTHOR=
# The public repository, its clone here, and the branch the night replaces.
# NIGHTLY_PUBLIC_REMOTE=https://github.com/BRF-Tech/filex.git
# NIGHTLY_PUBLIC_DIR=/var/lib/filex-nightly/public
# NIGHTLY_PUSH_BRANCH=nightly
# Where the push is made from. Empty: from the clone above, with this host's
# own git credential for the public repository, through the export gate
# (scripts/hooks/export-pre-push.sh, which needs gitleaks here). A container
# that holds the credential - the release workspace: the night's commit goes
# in as a bundle and scripts/chain/nightly-push.sh pushes it there, from a
# clone of its own, under NIGHTLY_PUSH_WRAP, the command that hands git the
# workspace's GitHub token for that one push. The token never leaves it.
# NIGHTLY_PUSH_CONTAINER=
# NIGHTLY_PUSH_USER=
# NIGHTLY_PUSH_WRAP=with-gh-token
# Inside the container: its clone of the public repository, and the private
# checkout the export gate reads its lists from (the release workspace's
# own; nothing in it is changed).
# NIGHTLY_PUSH_DIR=~/.cache/filex-nightly/public
# NIGHTLY_PUSH_GATE_SRC=~/filex
# skip: no push while GitHub tests a release (release.yml, or ci.yml on a
# push of main): the night's full matrix would share the organisation's 20
# jobs at once with the release's gate, and the next night pushes instead.
# push: push anyway. --force pushes anyway too.
# NIGHTLY_RELEASE_BUSY=skip

# ── GitHub ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The repository, its CI workflow (whose verdict the report reads: `All tests
# (full)` and every part) and the nightly workflow that builds the image and
# the desktop packages.
# NIGHTLY_GITHUB_REPO=BRF-Tech/filex
# NIGHTLY_CI_WORKFLOW=ci.yml
# NIGHTLY_DESKTOP_WORKFLOW=nightly-desktop.yml
# A file holding a GitHub token, sent with the API's reads for the rate limit
# only - everything read is public, so any token will do (0600). Without one,
# the API's anonymous limit, which a host behind a shared address may find used.
# NIGHTLY_GITHUB_TOKEN_FILE=/var/lib/filex-nightly/github.token
# The nightly image and the desktop packages' artifact on ghcr, the snap,
# and the ORAS client that reads them (a container, pinned).
# NIGHTLY_IMAGE_REPO=ghcr.io/brf-tech/filex
# NIGHTLY_DESKTOP_REPO=ghcr.io/brf-tech/filex-desktop-nightly
# NIGHTLY_SNAP_NAME=filex-app
# NIGHTLY_ORAS_IMAGE=ghcr.io/oras-project/oras:v1.2.2
# github: the morning follows GitHub's desktop packages up and puts them on
# filex.sh/nightly; off: neither.
# NIGHTLY_DESKTOP=github
# The command that publishes the page and the packages, given the directory
# the page was made in (sh -c '<command> "$1"'); NIGHTLY_SITE_REF names the
# artifact. The repository's own: scripts/chain/nightly-site.sh, installed
# beside the nightly (the site host pulls the packages from ghcr itself):
# NIGHTLY_SITE_CMD=bash /var/lib/filex-nightly/bin/nightly-site.sh --ssh <site host> --path <site directory>
# Empty: the page is made and kept in NIGHTLY_DESKTOP_DIR/site, and the report
# says it was not published.
# NIGHTLY_SITE_CMD=
# NIGHTLY_DESKTOP_DIR=/var/lib/filex-nightly/desktop

# ── the morning report ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One JSON POST (group, source, severity, title, message) with a Bearer key
# read from CHAIN_NOTIFY_KEY_FILE (never logged).
# CHAIN_NOTIFY_URL=https://notify.example.com/api/notify/v1/send
# CHAIN_NOTIFY_KEY_FILE=/var/lib/filex-nightly/notify.key
# NIGHTLY_NOTIFY_GROUP=infra
# NIGHTLY_NOTIFY_SOURCE=filex-nightly
# Minutes the report waits for a night still going; hours after which a
# night's record is not tonight's any more.
# NIGHTLY_REPORT_WAIT_MIN=30
# NIGHTLY_REPORT_MAX_AGE_H=20

# ── what does not run at night any more ──────────────────────────────────────
# The chain's nightly profile - the full chain plus ds-go, s3-live, shots and
# realenv (scripts/chain/nightly-lib.mjs NIGHTLY_EXTRAS) - is a person's run
# now, on this host, with a chain settings file (scripts/chain/chain.env.example):
#   bash scripts/chain/run.sh --profile nightly --env <file>
# The live S3 tests alone, when the morning report says the S3 code changed:
#   CHAIN_EXTRAS=s3-live bash scripts/chain/run.sh --profile targeted --env <file with FILEX_TEST_S3_*>
